# Build context for Dockerfile.demo ONLY — BuildKit reads <Dockerfile>.dockerignore in
# place of the repository's .dockerignore. That one excludes docs/ for the module
# images; this image needs exactly the fixtures and the script, so it is an
# allow-list: nothing else, and never a .env, can reach this image's layers.
*
!docs/schemas/fixtures
!docker/demo.sh
